"$$$/Premiere/Libraries/Dialogs/ConvertProjectDialog/BetaFeatureDesc=We now provide an option to delete media cache files when upgrading a project created in an older version of Premiere Pro. This can fix stability and playback issues. Media cache files are generated to help speed up playback of media files. For example, audio waveforms are cached in peak files. Occasionally, we need to make slight changes to the structure of these cache files like when we add support for a new format. As a result, cache files generated in older versions of Premiere Pro can sometimes create conflicts in newer versions and cause playback issues like stuttering, dropped frames, the wrong frames getting played back or complete playback failure. Deleting the media cache is a well understood troubleshooting step by experts. This will make the process easier for everyone."
"$$$/Premiere/Libraries/Dialogs/ConvertProjectDialog/BetaFeatureName=Option to clear media cache on project upgrades"
